{"name":"Tyrol","hex":"#b3cdbf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tyrol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A state in western Austria. Capital: Innsbruck.","A geographic region in Central Europe including the state of Tyrol in Austria and the regions of South Tyrol and Trentino in Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tyrol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tyrol","blocks":[{"text":"Tyrol is a historical region in the Alps of Northern Italy and western Austria. The area was historically the core of the County of Tyrol, part of the Holy Roman Empire, Austrian Empire and Austria-Hungary, from its formation in the 12th century until 1919."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg/330px-Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrol"},{"title":"Tyrol (state)","blocks":[{"text":"Tyrol is an Austrian state. It consists of two non-contiguous parts, North Tyrol and East Tyrol, separated by the Austrian state of Salzburg and the Italian province of South Tyrol, which was part of Tyrol until 1919. It is a constituent part of the present-day Euroregion Tyrol–South Tyrol–Trentino. The capital of Tyrol is Innsbruck."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg/330px-Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrol_(state)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tirol-Tirol_del_Sur-Trentino.png/330px-Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tirol-Tirol_del_Sur-Trentino.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tirol-Tirol_del_Sur-Trentino.png/330px-Eurorreg